  "design": [
    "Core captured error metadata shares immutable compiler text, owns no guest objects and survives collection or duplicate filenames. Current activation fallback never invokes guest stack/proxy/name hooks.",
    "Source positions derive from actual captured records; Node projects null-prototype metadata, zero-based start columns and undefined unnamed-eval resources.",
    "Unchanged configured Acorn is embedded through the existing shared dependency table for original Node assertion expression extraction.",
    "Exit-code and compile-cache protocol tables derive from configured SDK macro owners, retaining original descriptors, ordering and binding identity. This does not implement compile-cache operations.",
    "Caller location projects genuine VM activations and compilation origin, without fabricated bootstrap frames or stack hooks.",
    "Promises glob materializes the actual unchanged SDK export as a lazy data property, preserving descriptors and OS binding-capture order without eagerly importing readline/history."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "All-parallel goal remains open; latest frozen e9 stable full is1791/5015 and pinned full is1821/4727, both from immutable e9. No selected-case sums substituted.",
    "No speed claim; concurrent compilation/audits and actual instruction/RSS screen diagnostics retained.",
    "Initial all-API run377pass/1fail: the unchanged500ms child-liveness probe did not receive a PID under the concurrent pinned full audit. Isolated unchanged control passed2.10s; a full unchanged-source rerun after audits is retained separately. No deadline or assertion changed.",
    "Initial source binding check had incorrect descriptor-helper calls, retained and corrected. First focused attempt exposed missing Acorn dependency; the assertion comparison was preserved and dependency owner fixed.",
    "Initial Core attempt659pass/1fail used embedding eval in a new test while expecting Script origin. Corrected test uses the explicit Script API and adds separate eval-origin assertions; original failed result retained.",
    "Original node:test harness now progresses through genuine protocol/caller bindings to the missing native ContextifyScript; no fake VM class, callback, handle or compile-cache operation was introduced.",
    "Regular-file stdin on stock Node loads OS before input execution, unlike -e or piped stdin; oracle mode controls are retained. All four qualified API comparisons use the same -e mode as the established runner."
  ],
